WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.680
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.510
Jessica Jones, the wise-crackin', hard-drinkin',
private investigatin' superhero, is back for

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.719
a kick-ass second season, and with Avengers:
Infinity War just around the corner the show

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:16.800
has some awesome easter eggs and teases for
the Avengers' epic showdown with Thanos.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.390
Plus, there are some cool deep-cut Marvel
references which I'll be explaining.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.680
My new Marvel giveaway is also starting for
all my subscribers so keep watching and I'll

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.610
have more details on that later.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:32.580
Obviously, there are some spoilers for Season
2, so take care if you're not caught up.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:37.220
There are some great hat-tips to Avengers:
Infinity War, previous Marvel movie team-ups,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.640
and the comics when Jessica lets herself into
Oscar's apartment to look for clues only to

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.110
find his young son, Vido, awake.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.090
"Do you have any cool toys in your room you
wanna show me?"

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.790
"Do you know Captain America?"

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.510
"I got his action figure, but I lost the shield."

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.260
"So I made him a new one."

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.440
"All by myself."

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.239
"I just glued a magnet to it so it looks like
the real one."

00:00:58.239 --> 00:00:59.239
"Cap's shield is cooler."

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:02.810
"But this one doesn't have to take down any
aliens, so it'll do."

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.220
There's quite a lot of references here, so
let's break them down.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.650
Vido's holding a Captain America figure dressed
in what looks like his classic colours which

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.990
we saw him wear in Civil War.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.580
This isn't the first time we've seen how popular
Cap is with kids in Jessica's world as, in

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.350
Season 1, we saw a young child wearing a Captain
America costume in the park when Jessica first

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.510
tried to abduct Kilgrave.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:28.970
Back to this season: Vido's line about losing
Cap's shield is a delightful nod to the fact

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.860
that Captain America abandoned his shield
at the end of Civil War following his full-on

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.220
battle with Iron Man.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.060
"That shield doesn't belong to you."

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.530
"You don't deserve it!"

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:47.530
"My father made that shield!"

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:52.640
But Vido's words are also a shout-out to Avengers:
Infinity War where we'll likely see Cap without

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.280
a shield for a period of time.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.640
"Get this man a shield!"

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.210
But thanks to a certain genius by the name
of Shuri and some super-cutting-edge Wakandan

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.500
tech, Infinity War will also debut Cap's epic
new arm shields.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.630
And, frankly, I cannot wait!

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.260
By the way, I talk in detail about Cap's new
gauntlets, including how they compare to the

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.790
comics, in my video about Cap's new shield.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:19.540
Now, the fact Vido has created a replacement
shield for his Captain America figure using

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.959
a magnet is also a hat-tip to both the MCU
and comics where we've seen Cap throw his

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:28.409
shield around and call it back using magnetic
elements.

00:02:28.409 --> 00:02:33.450
Vido also says Cap's real shield is cooler
than the one he's made and adds, 'but this

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.879
one doesn't have to take down any aliens.'

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:40.609
Well, if Vido loves Cap's multi-coloured shield
which he used to kick alien Chitauri butt

00:02:40.609 --> 00:02:44.500
in the first Avengers movie, just wait till
he gets an eye-full of his new monochrome

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.480
shield in action in Infinity War where it
will most definitely be used to take down

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.560
some major alien threats from the likes of
Thanos's Black Order and those four-armed

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.019
creatures called Outriders.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:58.799
And then there's Vido's question to Jessica,
'Do you know Captain America?'

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:02.049
Jessica's hesitation in replying here is a
hint to the comics.

00:03:02.049 --> 00:03:06.340
The MCU's Jessica certainly does know of Steve
Rogers and the Avengers, just like the rest

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.349
of New York, for example, in Season 1, she
referred to 'the flag waver' and 'the big

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:11.540
green guy', in other words, Captain America
and the Hulk.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:16.939
But it's in Marvel's comics where Jessica
Jones actually does know Captain America personally.

00:03:16.939 --> 00:03:21.730
In early issues of the Alias comics, Jessica
inadvertently captures Captain America's secret

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.099
identity on film while she's on a case for
a client.

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:30.139
When she realises she's been set up to catch
Cap on camera, Jessica keeps the tape safe

00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:34.839
until she can hand it over to Steve Rogers
himself, who praises her for helping him,

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:39.719
and tells her to get in touch if she needs
anything or decides to be a superhero again.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.120
And in the What If?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.669
series, Jessica not only joined the Avengers
but she actually ended up marrying Steve Rogers!

00:03:46.669 --> 00:03:50.919
On top of that, in certain comics, the mantle
of Captain America is taken on by Jessica's

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:53.669
daughter with Luke Cage: Danielle.

00:03:53.669 --> 00:04:00.099
"If you say 'with great power comes great
responsibility', I swear I'll throw up."

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:05.760
Jessica also drops several sardonic references
to Spider-Man during season 2, including plays

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.430
on the line, 'With great power comes great
responsibility'

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.849
"You're always saying how powers are good
but you were wrong."

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:13.529
"What?!"

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:18.650
"With great power comes great mental illness."

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.340
And puns on Peter Parker's Spidey-sense.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.000
"I know she's in trouble."

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.000
"Because of your scroty-sense?"

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.200
"Goddamm right."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.760
Of course, Spider-Man is part of the Marvel
Cinematic Universe now, but even before his

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:35.040
first MCU appearance in Civil War, the creators
of Jessica Jones were already sneaking easter

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.430
eggs to the web-crawling superhero into their
first season.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.450
Yes, if you look really carefully, you can
see an ice-cream cart which was selling Spider-Man

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.600
ice cream!

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.660
As for this season's more overt shout-outs
to Spidey, they're a call-back to Jessica's

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.080
comic-book history with our friendly neighbourhood
Spider-Man.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.120
Given TV Jessica's sarcastic tone when she
talks about Spidey, it's actually quite funny

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.250
that in the comics her dad didn't seem to
have a very high opinion of the young web-slinger

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.250
either.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:07.250
As for Jessica's various mentions of Spider-Man's
famous mantra in the show, that has a special

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:10.020
significance if you dive back into the comics.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.510
In the books, after Jessica got her super-powers,
it was seeing Spidey take on the villainous

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.530
Sandman at her school that inspired her to
become a hero like him.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.740
And when she tells Spidey what an enormous
impact he had on her life, he shares with

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.080
her the saying that he lives his life by:
'with great power there must also come great

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.960
responsibility'.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.890
Jessica then tells him that she'll teach the
meaning of those words to her daughter, Danielle,

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:38.340
who, as I mentioned earlier, in some comics,
grows up to take on the role of Captain America.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:42.970
And in addition to that, it's Spider-Man who
encourages Jessica to go back to being a superhero

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:43.970
again.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:48.180
"Well I was buying whiskey at this liquor
store, and this guy came in."

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:54.530
"He was all jumpy and dope-sick and I knew
he was there to rob the place."

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.530
"Because of your spidey-sense?"

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:56.530
"I don't have spidey-sense.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.270
And that's far from the only connection between
Peter Parker and Jessica in the comics as

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.440
not only did they go to the same high school,
but she also had a quite a crush on him.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.600
In fact, she was about to ask him out when
things started to go radioactive for Peter!

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.500
Now, while it would be fun to see Tom Holland's
new Spider-Man swing through Jessica Jones's

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.970
TV world, we're very unlikely ever to see
that happen; however, given the pair's rich

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:23.240
history in the comics, I'm sure we will get
plenty more Spidey-related references like

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:26.210
the ones I've talked about here in future
shows.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:30.930
And Jessica Jones doesn't just limit its connections
to the Marvel movie universe, but it also

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.270
has plenty of references to Marvel's Netflix
shows.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:38.491
When one of the cops interrogating Jess says,
"I know you people like to team up", it's

00:06:38.491 --> 00:06:42.810
a nod to Jessica's last appearance in The
Defenders where she joined forces with Daredevil,

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.130
Luke Cage and Iron Fist against the Hand.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:49.900
Plus, it's also a call-back to the first season
of Jessica Jones where she worked together

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:54.490
with Luke Cage, who offered his support again
to her at the very end of The Defenders series.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.420
"Try staying in touch Jess.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.510
You got friends."

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:02.690
"One of them is in Harlem."

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:07.530
And the cop's words also foreshadow Alisa's
suggestion to Jessica that they team up to

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.150
do good and the way they work together to
save the family whose car crashes with a truck

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:16.290
carrying chemicals, as happened to Jessica's
family in the comics.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.660
On top of that, the cop's line about superhero
team-ups is also a wink to the Avengers movies

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:24.740
as well as various incarnations of the Avengers
in the comic books some of which featured

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.330
Jessica Jones as part of the famous group
of superheroes.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:33.389
Oh, and when Jessica's former boyfriend, Sterling,
finds out that her middle name is Campbell,

00:07:33.389 --> 00:07:37.490
that's a hat-tip to the comics, where Jessica's
original surname was Campbell until she was

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:42.620
adopted by the Jones family after her biological
family died in a car accident.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:46.540
Speaking of Sterling, one of the guys who
threatens him wears a necklace with the number

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:51.810
23 on it and asks about Jessica, 'Can she
fly?', which is a clear shout-out to issue

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:56.940
23 of Alias where Jessica starts to fly but
ends up crash-landing in the river, though

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:00.930
later she flies again and manages to stop
a robbery by the former PI-turned-villain,

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:01.980
the Scorpion.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.330
Now, what did you think of Season 2 of Jessica
Jones?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.910
And did you spot any other cool MCU or comic-book
easter eggs?

